Description: interactive multi-host ping monitor with live TUI
 ping-bulk monitors multiple hosts simultaneously using a persistent
 ping subprocess per host.  Results are displayed in a continuously
 updated terminal interface with rolling history, colour-coded status,
 statistics columns, section folding, a scrollable event log, SSH-based
 remote monitoring, and TCP port checks.
 .
 The program is a single self-contained Python 3 script with no
 third-party Python dependencies.

Package: ping-bulk-kiosk
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ping-bulk (= ${binary:Version}),
 tmux,
 systemd,
Recommends:
 openssh-client,
 vlock | physlock,
Suggests:
 ping-bulk-doc,
Description: kiosk mode for ping-bulk on physical consoles
 Provides systemd service unit and hardened tmux configuration to run
 ping-bulk as the sole application on a physical console (e.g. /dev/tty1).
 .
 Users can monitor hosts and SSH into them, but cannot escape to an
 unrestricted shell.  Includes SSH key isolation, restricted editor,
 syslog audit trail, and blocked escape routes.

